{"id":"agents-root","ord":"a0","title":"Agents","desc":"Who can be dispatched, one node per agent, THE EXACT LAUNCH COMMAND in each note. Every launcher reads the agent's node before spawning and runs exactly what the note says — a missing node REFUSES the spawn loudly; nobody falls back to a machine default (the Fable burn, 2026-08-13, is why this file exists). Spawn shape: `kolu create --repo <repo> --worktree <branch> --json -- <command>`. When kolu grows a structured launch spec, these notes migrate into it."}
{"id":"agent-claude-opus","parent":"agents-root","ord":"a0","title":"claude-opus — the author agent","desc":"Command: `claude --model opus --dangerously-skip-permissions`\n\nClaude Code pinned to Opus, YOLO mode. The default author for dispatched lanes. Verify with the banner: it must say Opus, not the machine default."}
{"id":"agent-grok","parent":"agents-root","ord":"a1","title":"grok — reviewer","desc":"Command: `grok --always-approve`\n\nGrok CLI in always-approve mode. Reviews in a split terminal of the author's worktree; posts one review comment via gh; never edits, pushes, or merges."}
{"id":"agent-opencode","parent":"agents-root","ord":"a2","title":"opencode — reviewer","desc":"Command: `opencode`\n\nopencode TUI on its configured model (kimi-k3 via Juspay at last sighting — the config is opencode's own, not spelled here). Same reviewer contract as grok. Known quirk: has mislabeled itself \"codex\" in a posted review once; brief it to title reviews with its tool name."}
